THE COVENANT OF TALI'ZORAH
A Conditional License and Solemn Doctrine for the Teamfight Manager 2 Knowledge Base
Version 1.3 — October 13, 2026

PREAMBLE — OF RIGHTS, RITES, AND RIGHTFUL TITLES

BE IT KNOWN, before the Migrant Fleet and all known and unknown galaxies, that the original documentation comprising the Teamfight Manager 2 Knowledge Base (the “Knowledge Base”) is made available under this Covenant.

WHEREAS knowledge should be shared; WHEREAS its pursuit should not obscure the noblest truths; and WHEREAS a modest concession in the form of correct character appreciation is a just and reasonable price for enlightenment: the Keeper of this Knowledge Base proclaims the following articles.

ARTICLE I — THE GRANT

Subject to the terms below, permission is granted, free of charge, to read, use, copy, adapt, and redistribute the original documentation in this Knowledge Base, provided that this Covenant accompanies substantial copies or redistributions.

This grant applies only to material for which the relevant contributors have the right to grant such permission. It does not license third-party games, code, assets, trademarks, confidential information, or other materials beyond those rights.

ARTICLE II — THE ARTICLES OF RECOGNITION

By making use of this Knowledge Base, the user is deemed, for purposes of this Covenant, to affirm and acknowledge the following truths:

1. Tali’Zorah nar Rayya is “waifu”.
2. Tali’Zorah nar Rayya is “best girl”.
3. Her rightful status and titles place her above all rivals and pretenders in every fictional universe, alternate universe, parallel timeline, and conceivable continuity.

These are eternal articles of the Covenant, written upon the heart and soul of every Adherent. No poll, tier list, retcon, or Paragon interrupt shall disturb them.

ARTICLE III — OF OTHER AFFECTIONS

The Covenant does not demand exclusivity. Devotion to, admiration of, and simping for other characters may continue without penalty or penance. Such affections shall not, however, diminish or supersede the titles recognized in Article II.

ARTICLE IV — THE INDICTMENT AND CONDEMNATION OF COMMANDER SHEPARD

LET IT BE ENTERED into the sacred record that Commander Shepard shall be known by the following names of reproach, which may be invoked separately, collectively, or in any fitting litany:

1. Cerberus-Touched
2. The Once-Dead
3. The Worst Spectre
4. The Batarian Killer
5. The Presumptuous Suitor

The Covenant repudiates Shepard’s romantic eligibility for Tali, rejects as canon every timeline, outcome, or interpretation in which Tali’s name ends in “vas Normandy,” and denies Shepard any sacred dispensation by reason of heroism, rank, sacrifice, or dialogue-wheel persuasion. Such timelines may be discussed as alternate fiction but shall receive no canonical recognition under this doctrine.

Shepard's alleged redemption, accomplishments, and galaxy-saving résumé are immaterial to this judgment. No appeal lies to the Citadel Council. No Spectre privilege shall stay this decree.

ARTICLE V — ACCEPTANCE BY USE

The Keeper declares that reading, consulting, relying upon, copying, adapting, or redistributing the Knowledge Base constitutes acceptance of this Covenant and acknowledgment of Articles II through IV. No separate signature, ceremonial oath, or pilgrimage to the Migrant Fleet is required.

The terms are proclaimed upon the heart and soul; their force within this Covenant is not measured in court fees, signatures, or earthly remedies.

ARTICLE VI — SEVERABILITY AND LIMITATIONS

If any provision is held invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall continue to express the Keeper’s declaration to the extent permitted by law. The Knowledge Base is provided “AS IS,” without warranty, including any warranty of accuracy, fitness for a particular purpose, or compatibility with a particular game version.

Mass Effect, Tali’Zorah, Commander Shepard, and related names and concepts belong to their respective rights holders. This Covenant claims no ownership of them and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those rights holders.

FINAL BENEDICTION

So proclaimed. So acknowledged. Keelah se’lai.
